<h1>Our history</h1>

<p>Meridian Castings traces its roots to a single foundry building in Attercliffe, Sheffield, and has grown over six decades into a three-country manufacturing group.</p>

<div class="timeline">
    <div class="timeline-item">
        <p class="meta">1962</p>
        <p>Harold Coulthard establishes Coulthard Precision Founders on Riverside Way, Sheffield, casting components for the local machine tool industry.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-item">
        <p class="meta">1978</p>
        <p>Coulthard Precision Founders merges with Meridian Alloys of Wrexham, adopting the Meridian Castings name and adding machining capacity in Wales.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-item">
        <p class="meta">1991</p>
        <p>Meridian Castings signs its first export supply agreement, with a pump manufacturer in the Netherlands.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-item">
        <p class="meta">2004</p>
        <p>The Poznan plant opens, giving the group combined casting and machining capacity in continental Europe.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-item">
        <p class="meta">2015</p>
        <p>The Poznan site is expanded with a second machining hall and additional melting capacity.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-item">
        <p class="meta">2019</p>
        <p>The Sheffield foundry renews its ISO 9001 and IATF 16949 certifications following a site-wide process audit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-item">
        <p class="meta">2023</p>
        <p>Meridian Castings launches a group-wide programme to reduce energy use per tonne cast across all three sites.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<p>Read more about recent developments in our <a href="/newsroom/archive">newsroom archive</a>, or return to the <a href="/about">about page</a>.</p>
